From 0e1a87ad34b3728d77d3a3407d2735f043f0e49b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hardening <hardening@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:34:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] web: ship the logo at display size, and serve WebP when
 the browser takes it

logo.png was a 1920x1920 RGBA render (492 KB) used as a 40 px sidebar mark, a
160 px login mark, and the favicon. It was the single largest item on the page:
32% of the 1.55 MB asset budget, and incompressible, so it outweighed the entire
gzip saving from the caching work in 1250320.

- public/logo.png   1920 -> 512 (3x the largest 160 px display)   492 KB -> 71 KB
- public/logo.webp  new, same 512 art                             492 KB -> 28 KB
- app/icon.png      1920 -> 192 (favicon)                         492 KB -> 17 KB
- app/apple-icon.png new, 180 (iOS home screen)

The three <img src=/logo.png> sites are wrapped in <picture> with a WebP source
and the PNG as fallback, so no component or CSS changes were needed.
---
 web/public/logo.png                           | Bin 492065 -> 72373 bytes
 web/public/logo.webp                          | Bin 0 -> 28778 bytes
 web/src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx             |   2 +-
 web/src/app/(auth)/setup/page.tsx             |   2 +-
 .../_components/sidebar/app-sidebar.tsx       |   2 +-
 web/src/app/apple-icon.png                    | Bin 0 -> 16293 bytes
 web/src/app/icon.png                          | Bin 492065 -> 17781 bytes
 7 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 web/public/logo.webp
 create mode 100644 web/src/app/apple-icon.png

diff --git a/web/public/logo.png b/web/public/logo.png
index d449f2529f73cce6de8306597027ac97d0add5f4..3cab9c9502ba3365fc602f2cdf6f446caa27a1f6 100644
GIT binary patch
